{"h": [{"text": "", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"sprite": "item/writable_book", "atlas": "minecraft:items", "color": "white"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#7a1f1f", "bold": true}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.guide", "fallback": "Guide", "color": "#7a1f1f", "bold": true}, {"text": "                           "}], "e": [{"k": {"text": "", "extra": [{"sprite": "item/iron_sword", "atlas": "minecraft:items", "color": "white"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#3a2614", "bold": true}, {"translate": "pnp.book.common.villagers", "fallback": "Villagers", "color": "#3a2614", "bold": true}, {"text": "\n"}, {"text": "  "}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.drop_a_weapon_armor_or_talisman", "fallback": "Drop a weapon, armor, or talisman \n  on a villager, iron golem, or wolf to \n  equip it, and hover them to see their \n  slots. Drop food on a hurt fighter \n  to heal them, even in the middle of a \n  fight.", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"text": "\n"}, {"text": "\n"}]}}, {"k": {"text": "", "extra": [{"sprite": "item/cooked_porkchop", "atlas": "minecraft:items", "color": "white"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#3a2614", "bold": true}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.supper", "fallback": "Supper", "color": "#3a2614", "bold": true}, {"text": "\n"}, {"text": "  "}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.at_dawn_every_villager_needs_2", "fallback": "At dawn every villager needs 2 \n  food points from your table, and \n  babies need 1. The cheapest food is \n  eaten first, and food in barrels \n  counts too. Cooking makes food \n  worth far more: a raw porkchop is 2 \n  points, cooked it's 6, and Cake is 16.", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"text": "\n"}, {"text": "\n"}]}}], "t": {"text": "", "extra": [{"text": "                     - 7 -", "color": "#7a6650"}, {"text": "\n                                                 "}]}, "L": [{}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}]},\
{"h": [{"text": "", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"sprite": "item/writable_book", "atlas": "minecraft:items", "color": "white"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#7a1f1f", "bold": true}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.guide", "fallback": "Guide", "color": "#7a1f1f", "bold": true}, {"text": "                           "}], "e": [{"k": {"text": "", "extra": [{"sprite": "item/pillager_spawn_egg", "atlas": "minecraft:items", "color": "white"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#3a2614", "bold": true}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.raids", "fallback": "Raids", "color": "#3a2614", "bold": true}, {"text": "\n"}, {"text": "  "}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.raiders_come_on_your_table_s", "fallback": "Raiders come on your table's \n  second night, then every third night \n  after that, and each raid is a little \n  tougher than the last. Patrols can \n  turn up during the day. From raid 5 \n  an Evoker joins in: it hangs back \n  casting fangs and calls Vexes when \n  it's hurt. Raid 10 brings the \n  Illusioner, and the raids keep \n  coming after that.", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"text": "\n"}, {"text": "\n"}]}}], "t": {"text": "\n\n\n\n\n", "extra": [{"text": "                     - 8 -", "color": "#7a6650"}, {"text": "\n                                                 "}]}, "L": [{}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}]},\
{"h": [{"text": "", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"sprite": "item/writable_book", "atlas": "minecraft:items", "color": "white"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#7a1f1f", "bold": true}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.guide", "fallback": "Guide", "color": "#7a1f1f", "bold": true}, {"text": "                           "}], "e": [{"k": {"text": "", "extra": [{"sprite": "item/iron_pickaxe", "atlas": "minecraft:items", "color": "white"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#3a2614", "bold": true}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.the_world", "fallback": "The world", "color": "#3a2614", "bold": true}, {"text": "\n"}, {"text": "  "}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.chopping_mining_and_harvesting_out_in", "fallback": "Chopping, mining, and harvesting out \n  in the world gives you cards. \n  Right-click a villager or animal with \n  the Card Board to bring it onto \n  your table.", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"text": "\n"}, {"text": "\n"}]}}, {"k": {"text": "", "extra": [{"sprite": "block/barrel_side", "atlas": "minecraft:blocks", "color": "white"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#3a2614", "bold": true}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.selling", "fallback": "Selling", "color": "#3a2614", "bold": true}, {"text": "\n"}, {"text": "  "}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.drop_cards_on_the_sell_box", "fallback": "Drop cards on the Sell box or a \n  Market to sell them. A card's tooltip \n  shows what it's worth. A Trading \n  Post swaps 9 emeralds for an \n  Emerald Block and back, and shops \n  count an Emerald Block as 9 \n  emeralds. Diamonds are for \n  crafting, not selling.", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"text": "\n"}, {"text": "\n"}]}}], "t": {"text": "", "extra": [{"text": "                     - 9 -", "color": "#7a6650"}, {"text": "\n                                                 "}]}, "L": [{}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}]},\
{"h": [{"text": "", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"sprite": "item/writable_book", "atlas": "minecraft:items", "color": "white"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#7a1f1f", "bold": true}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.guide", "fallback": "Guide", "color": "#7a1f1f", "bold": true}, {"text": "                           "}], "e": [{"k": {"text": "", "extra": [{"sprite": "item/emerald", "atlas": "minecraft:items", "color": "white"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#3a2614", "bold": true}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.the_shop", "fallback": "The shop", "color": "#3a2614", "bold": true}, {"text": "\n"}, {"text": "  "}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.drop_emeralds_or_emerald_blocks_on", "fallback": "Drop emeralds on a pack in your \n  shop row to buy it, then right-click it \n  to open. Right-click a shop pack to \n  see its cards. Each pack's first \n  card is always its kind. Quests and \n  purchases unlock more packs.", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"text": "\n"}, {"text": "\n"}]}}, {"k": {"text": "", "extra": [{"sprite": "item/lead", "atlas": "minecraft:items", "color": "white"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#3a2614", "bold": true}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.tool_mode", "fallback": "Tool mode", "color": "#3a2614", "bold": true}, {"text": "\n"}, {"text": "  "}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.right_click_the_wrench_to_enter", "fallback": "Right-click the Wrench to enter tool \n  mode. Cards lock in place, the world \n  turns grey, and machines show their \n  ports: green for inputs, orange for \n  outputs. Right-click one port and \n  then another to link them. Left-click \n  a port to cut its link.", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"text": "\n"}, {"text": "\n"}]}}], "t": {"text": "", "extra": [{"text": "                    - 10 -", "color": "#7a6650"}, {"text": "\n                                                 "}]}, "L": [{}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}]},\
{"h": [{"text": "", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"sprite": "item/writable_book", "atlas": "minecraft:items", "color": "white"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#7a1f1f", "bold": true}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.guide", "fallback": "Guide", "color": "#7a1f1f", "bold": true}, {"text": "                           "}], "e": [{"k": {"text": "", "extra": [{"sprite": "item/hopper", "atlas": "minecraft:items", "color": "white"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#3a2614", "bold": true}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.machines", "fallback": "Machines", "color": "#3a2614", "bold": true}, {"text": "\n"}, {"text": "  "}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.trees_rocks_bushes_farms_and_animals", "fallback": "Trees, rocks, bushes, farms, and \n  animals push what they make out of \n  their output. Barrels store up to \n  128 of one kind of card, and \n  Copper Barrels hold 256. Furnaces \n  smelt ore and pork with coal or \n  wood. Hoppers pass cards along, \n  and a card dropped on one \n  becomes its filter. Link into the Sell \n  box to sell on its own, or into a \n  Bundle to send cards home. \n  Droppers deal cards out across 3 \n  outputs. Cards go to a matching \n  filter or barrel first, and anything \n  with nowhere to go waits by its \n  source.", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"text": "\n"}, {"text": "\n"}]}}], "t": {"text": "", "extra": [{"text": "                    - 11 -", "color": "#7a6650"}, {"text": "\n                                                 "}]}, "L": [{}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}]},\
{"h": [{"text": "", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"sprite": "item/writable_book", "atlas": "minecraft:items", "color": "white"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#7a1f1f", "bold": true}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.guide", "fallback": "Guide", "color": "#7a1f1f", "bold": true}, {"text": "                           "}], "e": [{"k": {"text": "", "extra": [{"sprite": "item/iron_chestplate", "atlas": "minecraft:items", "color": "white"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#3a2614", "bold": true}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.specialists", "fallback": "Specialists", "color": "#3a2614", "bold": true}, {"text": "\n"}, {"text": "  "}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.hover_a_villager_iron_golem_or", "fallback": "Hover a villager, iron golem, or wolf \n  to see three slots: a weapon or \n  tool, armor, and a talisman. Drop a \n  card on them to equip it, and click a \n  slot to take it back. A villager's tool \n  gives them a job. Pickaxes make \n  Miners, axes Lumberjacks, hoes \n  Farmers, shears Shepherds, and \n  rods Fishers. Swords make \n  Swordsmen; bows, crossbows, and \n  tridents make Archers; shields \n  make Guards, maces Brutes, and \n  spears Lancers. Hover an enemy to \n  see what it carries.", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"text": "\n"}, {"text": "\n"}]}}], "t": {"text": "\n", "extra": [{"text": "                    - 12 -", "color": "#7a6650"}, {"text": "\n                                                 "}]}, "L": [{}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}]},\
{"h": [{"text": "", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"sprite": "item/writable_book", "atlas": "minecraft:items", "color": "white"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#7a1f1f", "bold": true}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.guide", "fallback": "Guide", "color": "#7a1f1f", "bold": true}, {"text": "                           "}], "e": [{"k": {"text": "", "extra": [{"sprite": "item/oak_planks", "atlas": "minecraft:items", "color": "white"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#3a2614", "bold": true}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.table_size", "fallback": "Table size", "color": "#3a2614", "bold": true}, {"text": "\n"}, {"text": "  "}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.your_table_starts_at_18_by", "fallback": "Your table starts at 18 by 18. Every \n  10 card slots above 15 makes it 2 \n  wider, up to 30 by 30. Shelves give \n  10 slots, Vaults give 25, and each \n  boss trophy adds 2 more. For more \n  room, unlock the side table to the \n  left for 10 Emerald Blocks, then \n  grow it with Table Leaves.", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#3a2614"}]}}], "t": {"text": "\n\n\n\n\n\n", "extra": [{"text": "                    - 13 -", "color": "#7a6650"}, {"text": "\n                                                 "}]}, "L": [{}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}]},\
{"h": [{"text": "", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"sprite": "item/writable_book", "atlas": "minecraft:items", "color": "white"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#7a1f1f", "bold": true}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.guide", "fallback": "Guide", "color": "#7a1f1f", "bold": true}, {"text": "                           "}], "e": [{"k": {"text": "", "extra": [{"sprite": "item/bow", "atlas": "minecraft:items", "color": "white"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#3a2614", "bold": true}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.combat", "fallback": "Combat", "color": "#3a2614", "bold": true}, {"text": "\n"}, {"text": "  "}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.fights_happen_in_a_fight_box", "fallback": "Fights happen in a fight box. Drop a \n  fighter on an enemy to start one, \n  then drop more fighters into the \n  box to join. Enemies that wander \n  close join too, and the box grows \n  to fit everyone. Fighters take turns: \n  melee fighters lunge at their target \n  and archers shoot from the back \n  row. Drag a fighter out to pull them \n  from the fight. While your board is \n  closed, fights, and raiders move five \n  times slower.", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"text": "\n"}, {"text": "\n"}]}}], "t": {"text": "\n\n\n", "extra": [{"text": "                    - 14 -", "color": "#7a6650"}, {"text": "\n                                                 "}]}, "L": [{}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}]},\
{"h": [{"text": "", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"sprite": "item/writable_book", "atlas": "minecraft:items", "color": "white"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#7a1f1f", "bold": true}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.guide", "fallback": "Guide", "color": "#7a1f1f", "bold": true}, {"text": "                           "}], "e": [{"k": {"text": "", "extra": [{"sprite": "item/fermented_spider_eye", "atlas": "minecraft:items", "color": "white"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#3a2614", "bold": true}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.status_effects", "fallback": "Status effects", "color": "#3a2614", "bold": true}, {"text": "\n"}, {"text": "  "}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.some_enemies_leave_status_effects_shown", "fallback": "Some enemies leave status effects, \n  shown as an icon on the card and in \n  its tooltip. Bogged poison (it can't \n  kill), Strays slow attacks, Guardians \n  cause fatigue that slows work and \n  attacks, and Vexes weaken hits. The \n  Warden's blows and the Illusioner's \n  spell blind, so fighters miss half \n  their attacks. Effects wear off \n  after a few seconds.", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"text": "\n"}, {"text": "\n"}]}}], "t": {"text": "\n\n\n\n\n", "extra": [{"text": "                    - 15 -", "color": "#7a6650"}, {"text": "\n                                                 "}]}, "L": [{}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}]},\
{"h": [{"text": "", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"sprite": "item/writable_book", "atlas": "minecraft:items", "color": "white"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#7a1f1f", "bold": true}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.guide", "fallback": "Guide", "color": "#7a1f1f", "bold": true}, {"text": "                           "}], "e": [{"k": {"text": "", "extra": [{"sprite": "item/experience_bottle", "atlas": "minecraft:items", "color": "white"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#3a2614", "bold": true}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.levels", "fallback": "Levels", "color": "#3a2614", "bold": true}, {"text": "\n"}, {"text": "  "}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.villagers_earn_experience_from_work_and", "fallback": "Villagers earn experience from \n  work and fights, ranking up from \n  Novice to Apprentice, Journeyman, \n  Expert, and Master. The badge in the \n  card's corner shows their rank. \n  Each rank adds health, and \n  Journeymen and Masters work \n  faster.", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"text": "\n"}, {"text": "\n"}]}}], "t": {"text": "\n\n\n\n\n\n\n", "extra": [{"text": "                    - 16 -", "color": "#7a6650"}, {"text": "\n                                                 "}]}, "L": [{}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}]},\
{"h": [{"text": "", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"sprite": "item/writable_book", "atlas": "minecraft:items", "color": "white"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#7a1f1f", "bold": true}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.guide", "fallback": "Guide", "color": "#7a1f1f", "bold": true}, {"text": "                           "}], "e": [{"k": {"text": "", "extra": [{"sprite": "block/crying_obsidian", "atlas": "minecraft:blocks", "color": "white"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#3a2614", "bold": true}, {"translate": "pnp.book.common.gateways", "fallback": "Gateways", "color": "#3a2614", "bold": true}, {"text": "\n"}, {"text": "  "}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.finding_a_trial_chamber_deep_dark", "fallback": "Finding a Trial Chamber, Deep Dark, \n  Ocean Monument, or Woodland \n  Mansion out in the world puts an \n  Unstable Gateway on your table for \n  3 days. Stack villagers on it and \n  right-click to send them through. \n  They face three waves and then a \n  boss, healing a little between waves. \n  Win, and the loot comes home as one \n  stack and you learn that place's \n  Stable Portal: a villager, 4 \n  cobblestone, a diamond, and a key. \n  Each portal run costs a key: a Trial \n  Key, Echo Shard, Prismarine Shard, \n  or Emerald Block.", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"text": "\n"}, {"text": "\n"}]}}], "t": {"text": "", "extra": [{"text": "                    - 17 -", "color": "#7a6650"}, {"text": "\n                                                 "}]}, "L": [{}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}]},\
{"h": [{"text": "", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"sprite": "item/writable_book", "atlas": "minecraft:items", "color": "white"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#7a1f1f", "bold": true}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.guide", "fallback": "Guide", "color": "#7a1f1f", "bold": true}, {"text": "                           "}], "e": [{"k": {"text": "", "extra": [{"sprite": "item/creeper_spawn_egg", "atlas": "minecraft:items", "color": "white"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#3a2614", "bold": true}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.night", "fallback": "Night", "color": "#3a2614", "bold": true}, {"text": "\n"}, {"text": "  "}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.the_table_follows_the_world_s", "fallback": "The table follows the world's day \n  and night. At night monsters creep \n  onto your table: zombies, skeletons, \n  spiders, and creepers. Zombies and \n  skeletons burn away at dawn. A \n  Torch keeps monsters from \n  spawning within 4 blocks of it, and a \n  Copper Bulb within 8.", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"text": "\n"}, {"text": "\n"}]}}], "t": {"text": "\n\n\n\n\n\n\n", "extra": [{"text": "                    - 18 -", "color": "#7a6650"}, {"text": "\n                                                 "}]}, "L": [{}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}]},\
{"h": [{"text": "", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"sprite": "item/writable_book", "atlas": "minecraft:items", "color": "white"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#7a1f1f", "bold": true}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.guide", "fallback": "Guide", "color": "#7a1f1f", "bold": true}, {"text": "                           "}], "e": [{"k": {"text": "", "extra": [{"sprite": "item/bread", "atlas": "minecraft:items", "color": "white"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#3a2614", "bold": true}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.supper", "fallback": "Supper", "color": "#3a2614", "bold": true}, {"text": "\n"}, {"text": "  "}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.short_of_food_at_dawn_villagers", "fallback": "Short of food at dawn? Villagers \n  are fed one at a time. Anyone who \n  gets nothing starves to death, and \n  the one left with only part goes \n  Hungry: 2 damage and 1 less attack \n  until the next supper. If everyone \n  eats and at least half of it was \n  cooked or baked, they're Well Fed: \n  healed 2 and 1 more attack until the \n  next supper.", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"text": "\n"}, {"text": "\n"}]}}], "t": {"text": "\n\n\n\n\n", "extra": [{"text": "                    - 19 -", "color": "#7a6650"}, {"text": "\n                                                 "}]}, "L": [{}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}]},\
{"h": [{"text": "", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"sprite": "item/writable_book", "atlas": "minecraft:items", "color": "white"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#7a1f1f", "bold": true}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.guide", "fallback": "Guide", "color": "#7a1f1f", "bold": true}, {"text": "                           "}], "e": [{"k": {"text": "", "extra": [{"sprite": "item/writable_book", "atlas": "minecraft:items", "color": "white"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#3a2614", "bold": true}, {"translate": "pnp.book.common.quests", "fallback": "Quests", "color": "#3a2614", "bold": true}, {"text": "\n"}, {"text": "  "}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.your_quest_book_lies_open_on", "fallback": "Your Quest Book lies open on the \n  platform beside your table. The left \n  page shows only your current main \n  quest, what it needs and its reward. \n  The right page has three side \n  quests. Every 3 days at dawn, the \n  ones you haven't started are \n  swapped for new ones. To hand \n  cards in, drop them on the book. \n  Rewards appear just below it.", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"text": "\n"}, {"text": "\n"}]}}], "t": {"text": "\n\n\n\n\n", "extra": [{"text": "                    - 20 -", "color": "#7a6650"}, {"text": "\n                                                 "}]}, "L": [{}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}]},\
{"h": [{"text": "", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"sprite": "item/writable_book", "atlas": "minecraft:items", "color": "white"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#7a1f1f", "bold": true}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.guide", "fallback": "Guide", "color": "#7a1f1f", "bold": true}, {"text": "                           "}], "e": [{"k": {"text": "", "extra": [{"sprite": "item/cake", "atlas": "minecraft:items", "color": "white"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#3a2614", "bold": true}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.babies", "fallback": "Babies", "color": "#3a2614", "bold": true}, {"text": "\n"}, {"text": "  "}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.two_villagers_on_a_house_make", "fallback": "Two villagers on a house make a \n  Baby Villager. Add food too (bread, \n  3 sweet berries, a cooked porkchop \n  or 2 apples) and a grown villager \n  moves in instead. Babies can't work \n  or fight and monsters leave them \n  alone, but they need 1 food point \n  at supper. They grow up after 5 \n  minutes.", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"text": "\n"}, {"text": "\n"}]}}], "t": {"text": "\n\n\n\n\n\n", "extra": [{"text": "                    - 21 -", "color": "#7a6650"}, {"text": "\n                                                 "}]}, "L": [{}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}]},\
{"h": [{"text": "", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"sprite": "item/writable_book", "atlas": "minecraft:items", "color": "white"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#7a1f1f", "bold": true}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.guide", "fallback": "Guide", "color": "#7a1f1f", "bold": true}, {"text": "                           "}], "e": [{"k": {"text": "", "extra": [{"sprite": "item/name_tag", "atlas": "minecraft:items", "color": "white"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#3a2614", "bold": true}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.playing_together", "fallback": "Playing together", "color": "#3a2614", "bold": true}, {"text": "\n"}, {"text": "  "}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.right_click_another_player_with_your", "fallback": "Right-click another player with your \n  Card Board to join their table. \n  You'll use their cards and recipes, \n  join their fights, and fill their \n  quests. Sneak to go back. When \n  several players share a table, \n  each player's head floats above \n  their cursor. To trade, send cards \n  home with a Bundle, hand over the \n  items, and bring them back in \n  through a barrel. A server can \n  also run one shared table for \n  everyone.", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"text": "\n"}, {"text": "\n"}]}}], "t": {"text": "\n\n", "extra": [{"text": "                    - 22 -", "color": "#7a6650"}, {"text": "\n                                                 "}]}, "L": [{}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}]},\
{"h": [{"text": "", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"sprite": "item/writable_book", "atlas": "minecraft:items", "color": "white"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#7a1f1f", "bold": true}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.guide", "fallback": "Guide", "color": "#7a1f1f", "bold": true}, {"text": "                           "}], "e": [{"k": {"text": "", "extra": [{"sprite": "item/name_tag", "atlas": "minecraft:items", "color": "white"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#3a2614", "bold": true}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.renaming_villagers", "fallback": "Renaming villagers", "color": "#3a2614", "bold": true}, {"text": "\n"}, {"text": "  "}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.right_click_a_villager_to_rename", "fallback": "Right-click a villager to rename it. A \n  book appears in your hand: open it, \n  write the name on the first page \n  and press Done.", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"text": "\n"}, {"text": "\n"}]}}, {"k": {"text": "", "extra": [{"sprite": "item/map", "atlas": "minecraft:items", "color": "white"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#3a2614", "bold": true}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.grid_and_move_area", "fallback": "Grid and Move Area", "color": "#3a2614", "bold": true}, {"text": "\n"}, {"text": "  "}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.right_click_the_grid_in_hotbar", "fallback": "Right-click the Grid in hotbar slot 7 \n  to line every card up on the block \n  grid. While it's selected, cards you \n  drop snap to the grid too. To move \n  a whole group, use Move Area in \n  slot 6: right-click two corners and \n  everything inside follows your \n  cursor. Left-click to put it down, or \n  right-click to put it all back.", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"text": "\n"}, {"text": "\n"}]}}], "t": {"text": "", "extra": [{"text": "                    - 23 -", "color": "#7a6650"}, {"text": "\n                                                 "}]}, "L": [{}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}]},\
{"h": [{"text": "", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"sprite": "item/writable_book", "atlas": "minecraft:items", "color": "white"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#7a1f1f", "bold": true}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.guide", "fallback": "Guide", "color": "#7a1f1f", "bold": true}, {"text": "                           "}], "e": [{"k": {"text": "", "extra": [{"sprite": "item/brush", "atlas": "minecraft:items", "color": "white"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#3a2614", "bold": true}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.painting_the_table", "fallback": "Painting the table", "color": "#3a2614", "bold": true}, {"text": "\n"}, {"text": "  "}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.right_click_the_paintbrush_to_pick", "fallback": "Right-click the Paintbrush to pick a \n  color, then click two corners on \n  the table to paint that area. Keep \n  right-clicking to cycle colors. \n  Press Shift or left-click the brush \n  to stop painting.", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"text": "\n"}, {"text": "\n"}]}}, {"k": {"text": "", "extra": [{"sprite": "item/bundle", "atlas": "minecraft:items", "color": "white"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#3a2614", "bold": true}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.bringing_things_home", "fallback": "Bringing things home", "color": "#3a2614", "bold": true}, {"text": "\n"}, {"text": "  "}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.drop_cards_on_a_bundle_to", "fallback": "Drop cards on a Bundle to send \n  them home. Villagers arrive as real \n  villagers with their trades. \n  Enchanted Books, potions, and \n  Explorer Maps become the real \n  thing, and trinkets turn into charms \n  that work in your off hand.", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"text": "\n"}, {"text": "\n"}]}}], "t": {"text": "", "extra": [{"text": "                    - 24 -", "color": "#7a6650"}, {"text": "\n                                                 "}]}, "L": [{}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}]},\
{"h": [{"text": "", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"sprite": "item/writable_book", "atlas": "minecraft:items", "color": "white"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#7a1f1f", "bold": true}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.guide", "fallback": "Guide", "color": "#7a1f1f", "bold": true}, {"text": "                           "}], "e": [{"k": {"text": "", "extra": [{"sprite": "item/recovery_compass_16", "atlas": "minecraft:items", "color": "white"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#3a2614", "bold": true}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.waystones_and_graves", "fallback": "Waystones and graves", "color": "#3a2614", "bold": true}, {"text": "\n"}, {"text": "  "}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.craft_a_waystone_kit_send_it", "fallback": "Craft a Waystone Kit, send it home, \n  and right-click where you want a \n  waystone. It shows up on your table \n  too: right-click it there to leave the \n  table at that spot. With a Shrine on \n  your table, the things you drop \n  when you die land on it as a Grave.", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"text": "\n"}, {"text": "\n"}]}}], "t": {"text": "\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n", "extra": [{"text": "                    - 25 -", "color": "#7a6650"}, {"text": "\n                                                 "}]}, "L": [{}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}]},\
{"h": [{"text": "", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"sprite": "item/writable_book", "atlas": "minecraft:items", "color": "white"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#7a1f1f", "bold": true}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.guide", "fallback": "Guide", "color": "#7a1f1f", "bold": true}, {"text": "                           "}], "e": [{"k": {"text": "", "extra": [{"sprite": "item/carrot", "atlas": "minecraft:items", "color": "white"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#3a2614", "bold": true}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.farming", "fallback": "Farming", "color": "#3a2614", "bold": true}, {"text": "\n"}, {"text": "  "}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.put_a_villager_and_a_crop", "fallback": "Put a villager and a crop \n  on a Farm and they grow more of it. \n  Carrots, Potatoes, Sugar Cane, and \n  Cocoa Beans come back three for \n  one, Melon Slices four, Cactus, and \n  Pumpkins two. A Farm on its own \n  grows two Wheat. Bake potatoes and \n  cook meat in a furnace to make them \n  worth far more.", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"text": "\n"}, {"text": "\n"}]}}], "t": {"text": "\n\n\n\n\n\n", "extra": [{"text": "                    - 26 -", "color": "#7a6650"}, {"text": "\n                                                 "}]}, "L": [{}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}]},\
{"h": [{"text": "", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"sprite": "item/writable_book", "atlas": "minecraft:items", "color": "white"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#7a1f1f", "bold": true}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.guide", "fallback": "Guide", "color": "#7a1f1f", "bold": true}, {"text": "                           "}], "e": [{"k": {"text": "", "extra": [{"sprite": "block/tnt_side", "atlas": "minecraft:blocks", "color": "white"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#3a2614", "bold": true}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.creepers_and_tnt", "fallback": "Creepers and TNT", "color": "#3a2614", "bold": true}, {"text": "\n"}, {"text": "  "}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.creepers_walk_up_to_your_villagers", "fallback": "Creepers walk up to your villagers \n  and light their fuse. Drop any \n  villager or fighter on a Creeper to \n  finish it off before it blows, and it \n  leaves Gunpowder behind. Two \n  Gunpowder and two Sand make TNT: \n  drag it onto a fight or a monster to \n  deal 5 damage to every enemy close \n  by.", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"text": "\n"}, {"text": "\n"}]}}], "t": {"text": "\n\n\n\n\n\n", "extra": [{"text": "                    - 27 -", "color": "#7a6650"}, {"text": "\n                                                 "}]}, "L": [{}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}]},\
{"h": [{"text": "", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"sprite": "item/writable_book", "atlas": "minecraft:items", "color": "white"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#7a1f1f", "bold": true}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.guide", "fallback": "Guide", "color": "#7a1f1f", "bold": true}, {"text": "                           "}], "e": [{"k": {"text": "", "extra": [{"sprite": "block/redstone_ore", "atlas": "minecraft:blocks", "color": "white"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#3a2614", "bold": true}, {"translate": "pnp.card.redstone_caves.name", "fallback": "Redstone Caves", "color": "#3a2614", "bold": true}, {"text": "\n"}, {"text": "  "}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.the_redstone_caves_are_a_wave", "fallback": "The Redstone Caves are a wave \n  area: five waves of Redstone Cubes, \n  with Redstone Golems as minibosses. \n  Stack villagers on the card and \n  right-click to send them in. The card \n  never fades, so go back as often \n  as you like. Golems sometimes drop a \n  Charged Redstone Core.", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"text": "\n"}, {"text": "\n"}]}}], "t": {"text": "\n\n\n\n\n\n\n", "extra": [{"text": "                    - 28 -", "color": "#7a6650"}, {"text": "\n                                                 "}]}, "L": [{}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}]},\
{"h": [{"text": "", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"sprite": "item/writable_book", "atlas": "minecraft:items", "color": "white"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#7a1f1f", "bold": true}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.guide", "fallback": "Guide", "color": "#7a1f1f", "bold": true}, {"text": "                           "}], "e": [{"k": {"text": "", "extra": [{"sprite": "item/ender_eye", "atlas": "minecraft:items", "color": "white"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#3a2614", "bold": true}, {"translate": "pnp.card.redstone_monstrosity.name", "fallback": "Redstone Monstrosity", "color": "#3a2614", "bold": true}, {"text": "\n"}, {"text": "  "}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.stack_a_charged_redstone_core_with", "fallback": "Stack a Charged Redstone Core with \n  a Summoning Orb (Evokers sometimes \n  drop one). After 30 seconds the \n  Redstone Monstrosity bursts onto \n  your table. It slams the ground, \n  calls Redstone Cubes, and is \n  shielded while any of them live. Beat \n  it with your villagers to finish \n  Chapter 1.", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"text": "\n"}, {"text": "\n"}]}}], "t": {"text": "\n\n\n\n\n\n", "extra": [{"text": "                    - 29 -", "color": "#7a6650"}, {"text": "\n                                                 "}]}, "L": [{}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}]},\
{"h": [{"text": "", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"sprite": "item/writable_book", "atlas": "minecraft:items", "color": "white"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#7a1f1f", "bold": true}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.guide", "fallback": "Guide", "color": "#7a1f1f", "bold": true}, {"text": "                           "}], "e": [{"k": {"text": "", "extra": [{"sprite": "block/nether_portal", "atlas": "minecraft:blocks", "color": "white"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#3a2614", "bold": true}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.game_modes_and_pvp", "fallback": "Game modes and PvP", "color": "#3a2614", "bold": true}, {"text": "\n"}, {"text": "  "}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.when_a_world_starts_the_host", "fallback": "When a world starts, the host picks \n  how to play: Single Player, or \n  Multiplayer with a Shared Board, \n  Individual Boards or PvP. In PvP \n  your table gets a portal for every \n  other player, named after them. \n  Drop villagers, wolves, or golems on \n  a portal and right-click to send \n  them. They arrive at that table \n  right away. If they beat the \n  defenders, or are still standing \n  after 90 seconds, each one steals \n  a valuable card and they all come \n  home. A table that was just attacked \n  is safe for 5 minutes.", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"text": "\n"}, {"text": "\n"}]}}], "t": {"text": "", "extra": [{"text": "                    - 30 -", "color": "#7a6650"}, {"text": "\n                                                 "}]}, "L": [{}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}]},\
{"h": [{"text": "", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"sprite": "item/writable_book", "atlas": "minecraft:items", "color": "white"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#7a1f1f", "bold": true}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.guide", "fallback": "Guide", "color": "#7a1f1f", "bold": true}, {"text": "                           "}], "e": [{"k": {"text": "", "extra": [{"sprite": "block/netherrack", "atlas": "minecraft:blocks", "color": "white"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#3a2614", "bold": true}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.the_nether", "fallback": "The Nether", "color": "#3a2614", "bold": true}, {"text": "\n"}, {"text": "  "}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.the_nether_text", "fallback": "Build a Nether Portal from 10 \n  Obsidian and Flint and Steel, or \n  repair a Ruined Portal. Right-click \n  the portal to travel to your Nether \n  table, and stack cards on it to send \n  them across. Work the Nether Wastes \n  for gold. A villager with a Compass \n  on the Wastes finds a biome you \n  haven't seen. Food left on the \n  Nether table chars after 4 days, \n  worth half, then burns to Ash 4 \n  days later.", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"text": "\n"}, {"text": "\n"}]}}], "t": {"text": "\n\n\n", "extra": [{"text": "                    - 31 -", "color": "#7a6650"}, {"text": "\n                                                 "}]}, "L": [{}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}]},\
{"h": [{"text": "", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"sprite": "item/writable_book", "atlas": "minecraft:items", "color": "white"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#7a1f1f", "bold": true}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.guide", "fallback": "Guide", "color": "#7a1f1f", "bold": true}, {"text": "                           "}], "e": [{"k": {"text": "", "extra": [{"sprite": "item/gold_ingot", "atlas": "minecraft:items", "color": "white"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#3a2614", "bold": true}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.piglins_and_gold", "fallback": "Piglins and gold", "color": "#3a2614", "bold": true}, {"text": "\n"}, {"text": "  "}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.piglins_and_gold_text", "fallback": "Piglins attack villagers without gold. \n  Drop a Gold Ingot on one to barter \n  for a random card, or give it 3 at \n  once to recruit it. A Golden Helmet \n  keeps Piglins off its wearer, and a \n  Gilded Charm calms every Piglin on \n  the table. The Nether shop row \n  takes Gold Ingots, and each pack \n  unlocks the next. Now and then a \n  Piglin Merchant visits with rare \n  cards for 8 gold.", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"text": "\n"}, {"text": "\n"}]}}], "t": {"text": "\n\n\n\n", "extra": [{"text": "                    - 32 -", "color": "#7a6650"}, {"text": "\n                                                 "}]}, "L": [{}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}]},\
{"h": [{"text": "", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"sprite": "item/writable_book", "atlas": "minecraft:items", "color": "white"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#7a1f1f", "bold": true}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.guide", "fallback": "Guide", "color": "#7a1f1f", "bold": true}, {"text": "                           "}], "e": [{"k": {"text": "", "extra": [{"sprite": "item/blaze_rod", "atlas": "minecraft:items", "color": "white"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#3a2614", "bold": true}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.nether_gateways", "fallback": "Nether gateways", "color": "#3a2614", "bold": true}, {"text": "\n"}, {"text": "  "}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.nether_gateways_text", "fallback": "Nether Wastes trips can turn up a \n  Fortress gateway, guaranteed by \n  the 10th trip, and Crimson Forest \n  trips a Bastion by the 10th. The \n  Fortress ends with the Wildfire, \n  whose shields break fastest to \n  ranged attacks. The Bastion ends \n  with the Mutated Hoglin. Put 3 Wither \n  Skeleton Skulls on 4 Soul Sand to \n  summon the Wither. While it flies, only \n  ranged fighters can hurt it.", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"text": "\n"}, {"text": "\n"}]}}], "t": {"text": "\n\n\n\n", "extra": [{"text": "                    - 33 -", "color": "#7a6650"}, {"text": "\n                                                 "}]}, "L": [{}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}]},\
{"h": [{"text": "", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"sprite": "item/writable_book", "atlas": "minecraft:items", "color": "white"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#7a1f1f", "bold": true}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.guide", "fallback": "Guide", "color": "#7a1f1f", "bold": true}, {"text": "                           "}], "e": [{"k": {"text": "", "extra": [{"sprite": "item/brewing_stand", "atlas": "minecraft:items", "color": "white"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#3a2614", "bold": true}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.potions", "fallback": "Potions", "color": "#3a2614", "bold": true}, {"text": "\n"}, {"text": "  "}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.potions_text", "fallback": "Drop a potion on a villager to use it. \n  Healing heals 4, and Regeneration \n  heals 1 a second for 30 seconds. \n  Swiftness makes it work twice as \n  fast, Strength adds attack, Night \n  Vision stops blinding and Water \n  Breathing stops Guardian fatigue, all \n  until the next supper. Fire \n  Resistance stops fire damage for 3 \n  days. Or send a potion home in a \n  Bundle.", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"text": "\n"}, {"text": "\n"}]}}], "t": {"text": "\n\n\n\n", "extra": [{"text": "                    - 34 -", "color": "#7a6650"}, {"text": "\n                                                 "}]}, "L": [{}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}]},\
{"h": [{"text": "", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"sprite": "item/writable_book", "atlas": "minecraft:items", "color": "white"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#7a1f1f", "bold": true}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.guide", "fallback": "Guide", "color": "#7a1f1f", "bold": true}, {"text": "                           "}], "e": [{"k": {"text": "", "extra": [{"sprite": "item/book", "atlas": "minecraft:items", "color": "white"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#3a2614", "bold": true}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.orders_and_helpers", "fallback": "Orders and helpers", "color": "#3a2614", "bold": true}, {"text": "\n"}, {"text": "  "}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.orders_and_helpers_text", "fallback": "Once you have a Trading Post, it \n  posts an Order every few days: fill \n  it within 2 days for emeralds. Ender \n  Chests share one storage across \n  both tables. A Respawn Anchor \n  charged with Glowstone Dust brings \n  back a villager who falls on the \n  Nether table, but explodes on the \n  overworld table. The Barter Station, \n  Nether Wart Farm and Blaze Spawner \n  work on their own.", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"text": "\n"}, {"text": "\n"}]}}], "t": {"text": "\n\n\n\n", "extra": [{"text": "                    - 35 -", "color": "#7a6650"}, {"text": "\n                                                 "}]}, "L": [{}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}]},\
{"h": [{"text": "", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"sprite": "item/writable_book", "atlas": "minecraft:items", "color": "white"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#7a1f1f", "bold": true}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.guide", "fallback": "Guide", "color": "#7a1f1f", "bold": true}, {"text": "                           "}], "e": [{"k": {"text": "", "extra": [{"sprite": "item/filled_map", "atlas": "minecraft:items", "color": "white"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#3a2614", "bold": true}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.maps_and_counters", "fallback": "Maps and counters", "color": "#3a2614", "bold": true}, {"text": "\n"}, {"text": "  "}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.maps_and_counters_text", "fallback": "A villager with an explorer map \n  opens that map's gateway on your \n  table. Some rare finds keep count: \n  the action bar shows how many trips \n  are left until one is guaranteed. The \n  first trip to each Nether biome \n  brings its key cards. Side quests \n  appear once you have what they \n  need, and the first Wandering \n  Trader is announced the evening \n  before.", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"text": "\n"}, {"text": "\n"}]}}], "t": {"text": "\n\n\n\n", "extra": [{"text": "                    - 36 -", "color": "#7a6650"}, {"text": "\n                                                 "}]}, "L": [{}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}]},\
{"h": [{"text": "", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"sprite": "item/writable_book", "atlas": "minecraft:items", "color": "white"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#7a1f1f", "bold": true}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.guide", "fallback": "Guide", "color": "#7a1f1f", "bold": true}, {"text": "                           "}], "e": [{"k": {"text": "", "extra": [{"sprite": "item/saddle", "atlas": "minecraft:items", "color": "white"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#3a2614", "bold": true}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.lava_sea_and_nights", "fallback": "Lava Sea and nights", "color": "#3a2614", "bold": true}, {"text": "\n"}, {"text": "  "}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.lava_sea_and_nights_text", "fallback": "Put a Saddle on a Strider. With a \n  villager and a Warped Fungus on a \n  Stick, the Saddled Strider finds the \n  Lava Sea, then carries villagers out \n  to work it for gold, Ancient Debris \n  and treasure. Some Nether nights \n  bring a Ghast Storm or a Hoglin \n  Stampede, and Hoglins taken through \n  the portal turn into Zoglins.", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"text": "\n"}, {"text": "\n"}]}}], "t": {"text": "\n\n\n\n\n\n", "extra": [{"text": "                    - 37 -", "color": "#7a6650"}, {"text": "\n                                                 "}]}, "L": [{}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}]},\
{"h": [{"text": "", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"sprite": "item/writable_book", "atlas": "minecraft:items", "color": "white"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#7a1f1f", "bold": true}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.guide", "fallback": "Guide", "color": "#7a1f1f", "bold": true}, {"text": "                           "}], "e": [{"k": {"text": "", "extra": [{"sprite": "block/composter_side", "atlas": "minecraft:blocks", "color": "white"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#3a2614", "bold": true}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.composting_and_furnaces", "fallback": "Composting and furnaces", "color": "#3a2614", "bold": true}, {"text": "\n"}, {"text": "  "}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.composting_and_furnaces_text", "fallback": "A Composter turns every 4 crops, \n  fungi or Ash into Bone Meal. Drop \n  Bone Meal on a working Farm, tree, \n  bush or Nether forest to finish it \n  right away. A Smoker cooks food and \n  a Blast Furnace smelts ores twice \n  as fast as a Furnace. A Cobblestone \n  Generator makes Cobblestone on its \n  own.", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"text": "\n"}, {"text": "\n"}]}}], "t": {"text": "\n\n\n\n\n\n", "extra": [{"text": "                    - 38 -", "color": "#7a6650"}, {"text": "\n                                                 "}]}, "L": [{}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}]},\
{"h": [{"text": "", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"sprite": "item/writable_book", "atlas": "minecraft:items", "color": "white"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#7a1f1f", "bold": true}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.guide", "fallback": "Guide", "color": "#7a1f1f", "bold": true}, {"text": "                           "}], "e": [{"k": {"text": "", "extra": [{"sprite": "block/crying_obsidian", "atlas": "minecraft:blocks", "color": "white"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#3a2614", "bold": true}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.nether_automation", "fallback": "Nether automation", "color": "#3a2614", "bold": true}, {"text": "\n"}, {"text": "  "}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.nether_automation_text", "fallback": "The Wrench works on your Nether \n  table too. Pipe cards into a Nether \n  Portal and they come out of the \n  portal on your other table. Nether \n  nodes have output ports like the \n  overworld ones. A Brewing Stand \n  brews on its own from piped \n  ingredients, and Blaze Powder makes \n  it brew two at once.", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"text": "\n"}, {"text": "\n"}]}}], "t": {"text": "\n\n\n\n\n\n", "extra": [{"text": "                    - 39 -", "color": "#7a6650"}, {"text": "\n                                                 "}]}, "L": [{}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}]},\
{"h": [{"text": "", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"sprite": "item/writable_book", "atlas": "minecraft:items", "color": "white"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#7a1f1f", "bold": true}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.guide", "fallback": "Guide", "color": "#7a1f1f", "bold": true}, {"text": "                           "}], "e": [{"k": {"text": "", "extra": [{"sprite": "block/red_sand", "atlas": "minecraft:blocks", "color": "white"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#3a2614", "bold": true}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.new_lands", "fallback": "New lands", "color": "#3a2614", "bold": true}, {"text": "\n"}, {"text": "  "}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.new_lands_text", "fallback": "Visiting the Badlands, Snowy Plains \n  or a Swamp in your world puts its \n  card on your table. The Badlands \n  give gold and Terracotta, the Snowy \n  Plains give Ice, which halves \n  charring next to Nether food, and \n  the Swamp gives Slimeballs for Magma \n  Cream. Witches come at night once \n  you know a Swamp. A Horse in a \n  villager's talisman slot doubles its \n  node work speed.", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"text": "\n"}, {"text": "\n"}]}}], "t": {"text": "\n\n\n\n", "extra": [{"text": "                    - 40 -", "color": "#7a6650"}, {"text": "\n                                                 "}]}, "L": [{}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}]},\
{"h": [{"text": "", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"sprite": "item/writable_book", "atlas": "minecraft:items", "color": "white"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#7a1f1f", "bold": true}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.guide", "fallback": "Guide", "color": "#7a1f1f", "bold": true}, {"text": "                           "}], "e": [{"k": {"text": "", "extra": [{"sprite": "item/ominous_bottle", "atlas": "minecraft:items", "color": "white"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#3a2614", "bold": true}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.outposts_and_bogs", "fallback": "Outposts and bogs", "color": "#3a2614", "bold": true}, {"text": "\n"}, {"text": "  "}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.outposts_and_bogs_text", "fallback": "Finding a Pillager Outpost in your \n  world, or a lucky Adventure or \n  Combat Pack, gives an Outpost \n  gateway. Its Pillager Captain drops \n  an Ominous Bottle: right-click it and a \n  Captain's Raid hits your table at \n  nightfall. Working a Swamp can turn \n  up a Slime Bog gateway, home of the \n  Mega Slime.", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"text": "\n"}, {"text": "\n"}]}}], "t": {"text": "\n\n\n\n\n\n", "extra": [{"text": "                    - 41 -", "color": "#7a6650"}, {"text": "\n                                                 "}]}, "L": [{}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}]},\
{"h": [{"text": "", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"sprite": "item/writable_book", "atlas": "minecraft:items", "color": "white"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#7a1f1f", "bold": true}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.guide", "fallback": "Guide", "color": "#7a1f1f", "bold": true}, {"text": "                           "}], "e": [{"k": {"text": "", "extra": [{"sprite": "block/enchanting_table_top", "atlas": "minecraft:blocks", "color": "white"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#3a2614", "bold": true}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.enchanting", "fallback": "Enchanting", "color": "#3a2614", "bold": true}, {"text": "\n"}, {"text": "  "}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.enchanting_text", "fallback": "Stack a villager, Lapis Lazuli and a \n  weapon or armor on an Enchanting \n  Table. Weapons get Sharpness or \n  their own kind, worth +1 attack per \n  level. Armor gets Protection, +1 \n  health per level, or Fire Protection \n  against fire attacks. Enchant again \n  to reach level III. The enchantment \n  stays on the card, and a Bundle \n  exports it as the real enchanted \n  item.", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"text": "\n"}, {"text": "\n"}]}}], "t": {"text": "\n\n\n\n", "extra": [{"text": "                    - 42 -", "color": "#7a6650"}, {"text": "\n                                                 "}]}, "L": [{}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}]},\
{"h": [{"text": "", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"sprite": "item/writable_book", "atlas": "minecraft:items", "color": "white"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#7a1f1f", "bold": true}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.guide", "fallback": "Guide", "color": "#7a1f1f", "bold": true}, {"text": "                           "}], "e": [{"k": {"text": "", "extra": [{"sprite": "block/barrel_top_open", "atlas": "minecraft:blocks", "color": "white"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#3a2614", "bold": true}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.links_to_your_world", "fallback": "Links to your world", "color": "#3a2614", "bold": true}, {"text": "\n"}, {"text": "  "}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.links_to_your_world_text", "fallback": "Sneak and right-click a real barrel \n  with your Card Board to link it: a \n  Linked Barrel card appears on your \n  table. Right-click the card to switch \n  between pulling items in and sending \n  piped cards out to that barrel. \n  Place a real Lodestone anywhere, \n  even in the Nether, and that spot \n  becomes a waystone on your table.", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"text": "\n"}, {"text": "\n"}]}}], "t": {"text": "\n\n\n\n\n\n", "extra": [{"text": "                    - 43 -", "color": "#7a6650"}, {"text": "\n                                                 "}]}, "L": [{}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}]},\
{"h": [{"text": "", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"sprite": "item/writable_book", "atlas": "minecraft:items", "color": "white"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#7a1f1f", "bold": true}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.guide", "fallback": "Guide", "color": "#7a1f1f", "bold": true}, {"text": "                           "}], "e": [{"k": {"text": "", "extra": [{"sprite": "item/nether_star", "atlas": "minecraft:items", "color": "white"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#3a2614", "bold": true}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.nether_shops_and_beacon", "fallback": "Nether shops, Beacon", "color": "#3a2614", "bold": true}, {"text": "\n"}, {"text": "  "}, {"translate": "pnp.book.guide.nether_shops_and_beacon_text", "fallback": "The Nether shop row takes Gold \n  Ingots. The Wastes Pack is always \n  open. The Fortress Pack opens \n  after A Fortress in the Fire or 3 \n  Wastes Packs, and the Bastion Pack \n  after The Bastion or 3 Fortress \n  Packs. A Piglin Merchant visits by \n  day with one card for 8 gold. After \n  the Wither, its Nether Star builds a \n  Beacon: feed it minerals for a buff \n  on your table.", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"text": " ", "color": "#3a2614"}, {"text": "\n"}, {"text": "\n"}]}}], "t": {"text": "\n\n\n\n", "extra": [{"text": "                    - 44 -", "color": "#7a6650"}, {"text": "\n                                                 "}]}, "L": [{}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}]}]
